    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_1f0a5451dd3779d440a200fbdfdf5c691dbc20597ed726b7f1b39f6e40d2c350",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "For negative theta, the low-prime field is a nearly common mode across the short interval. Removing it is simultaneously a probabilistic coarse-graining of the branching picture and the analytic mollification that leaves an effective field of depth and variance 1+theta for moment optimization.",
