      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Inverse-log sampling is the recurring bridge from one-location moment or L2 estimates to interval-uniform bounds. A finite logarithmic-bandwidth polynomial is sampled on roughly interval length times log T sites, and the underlying estimate must contain enough slack to pay for that grid cardinality and the weighted tail.",
